From: Xios project <xios@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] i_main: mark SDL ready when built for Xios

xios-sdl2 is compiled for the iOS target, where SDL_Init() fails with
"Application didn't initialize properly" until SDL_SetMainReady() has run.
With CRISPY_XIOS the program keeps its own main(), so call it first thing.
OpenTTD and the xios-sdl smoke clients do the same.

--- a/src/i_main.c
+++ b/src/i_main.c
@@ -42,6 +42,14 @@
 
 int main(int argc, char **argv)
 {
+#ifdef CRISPY_XIOS
+    // [Xios] SDL is built for the iOS target, where it refuses SDL_Init()
+    // until SDL's own UIKit main trampoline has run. Xios runs this as an
+    // ordinary Unix Wayland client with its own main(), so mark SDL ready
+    // here, before anything initializes a subsystem.
+    SDL_SetMainReady();
+#endif
+
     // save arguments
 
     myargc = argc;
